      <p>Groups need different functions. Someone initiates, someone stabilizes, someone adapts, someone notices feelings, and someone asks hard questions. A lower-scoring pair may still be valuable because it adds contrast. A higher-scoring pair may still need boundaries if their shared energy overwhelms the rest of the room.</p>
